    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but therapy won't fix the fact that the \"me\" that mattered doesn't exist anymore. everything i loved was tied to what i could do, what my body could achieve. now i'm just... stuck in this thing that's broken and heavy. it feels like i'm just taking up space in a life that's already over.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's understandable that when your identity was so closely tied to your abilities, this loss feels absolute. However, healing is often about redefining who you are outside of what you can physically do. Therapy can help you gently explore new aspects of your identity that can thrive even when your physical capabilities have changed. These new definitions can create a new, meaningful sense of self within your current life.",
      "source": "target",
